																		2013 Guide Overhaul
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aelanna" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(334454); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=334454&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973998" alt="Aelanna" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=334454)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aelanna" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(334454); return false;" >Aelanna</a></span> <span class="odate time_1389421937 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jan 2014 06:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1933173">
									

<p>This guide has been rewritten as part of the 2014 background guide overhaul. The original version of this page can be found in archive form <a href="/task-forces-arc">here</a>.</p>
<h1><span>Removed and Renamed Entries</span></h1>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Alpha-2</strong> (&quot;The Mailmen&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only ever having had one SCP use its designation as described; all other mentions of &quot;Alpha-2&quot; were generic usages of Mobile Task Forces.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Alpha-16</strong> (&quot;Uncle Mike's&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP. One other instance of &quot;Alpha-16&quot; exists on-site but is unrelated and differently named.</li>
<li><strong>Task Force Alpha-440</strong> (&quot;What The Hell Was That Sound?&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being inconsistent with page usage.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Beta-3</strong> (&quot;Take-out Diners&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Task Force Delta-9</strong> (&quot;Hacks&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Iota-4</strong> (&quot;Dream Hunters&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Iota-5</strong> (&quot;Tiger Bait&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP with one additional generic and inconsistent reference.</li>
<li><strong>Reconnaissance Force Kappa-6</strong> (&quot;Angel Eyes&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only referring to a single SCP and a single tale hub.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Kappa-42</strong> (&quot;Lucky Seven&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to only being referred to in a single author profile page.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Lambda-2</strong> (&quot;Dr Clef's Bisexual All-Female Stripper Assassin Squad&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being hilarious but not much else.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Lambda-3</strong> (&quot;No Given Nickname&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Nu-1</strong> (&quot;Cause and Effective&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to no references in existence.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Nu-6</strong> (&quot;Triple-Dog Daredevils&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Xi-8</strong> (aka &quot;Spearhunters&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to strangely specific focus and only being referred to in two low-rated SCPs.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Xi-11</strong> (aka &quot;Polarbears&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to no references in existence.</li>
<li><strong>Armed Rapid Response Task Force Xi-13</strong> (&quot;Sequere Nos&quot; <em>[&quot;Follow Us&quot;]</em>) &#8212; Removed due to only being referenced in a single tale series.</li>
<li><strong>Reconnaissance Task Force Omicron-6U</strong> (&quot;Trilobite&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Omicron-9</strong> (&quot;Hot Zone Dancers&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to no references in existence.</li>
<li><strong>Rapid Response Task Force Omicron-11</strong> (&quot;Burke's Boys&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP. Also, the concept is quite silly.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Rho-5</strong> (&quot;Stitch In Time&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Rho-8</strong> (&quot;Roadside Picnickers&quot;) &#8212; Removed because the only explicit reference is a negation of necessity and the only nonexplicit reference is used in a generic form.</li>
<li><strong>Task Force Sigma-6</strong> (&quot;Puddlejumpers&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP and excessively legitimizing that canon. One additional reference exists but is inconsistent with this definition.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Upsilon-2</strong> (&quot;Cattlewranglers&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to being referred to in only a single SCP.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile Task Force Chi-7</strong> (&quot;Spotlight Specialists&quot;) &#8212; Removed due to no specific references in existence; only a single generic reference exists.</li>
</ul>
