<blockquote>
<p>It is less accessable than the old version.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't know what you mean by this. Rather than simply being a list of names and gratuitous links like the list used to be, now it's a general guide of how they can be created and used, along with an OOC writing guide that's useful to new members. Can you clarify?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It also makes the concept of MTF more rigid. It will mostly be useful by people who like this specific take.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I will have to respectfully disagree with you here; previously, there was absolutely zero description at all, and the common <em>interpretation</em> was that all Mobile Task Forces were comprised of soldiers. We've gone out of our way to fight that perception by stating that any group of specialists can be a Mobile Task Force. In fact, now I'm curious what your particular take on Mobile Task Forces are.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The decommision of &quot;Pandora's Box&quot; also seem bad. If the concept of Able's task force is no longer to be because it no longer fits the current foundation, it would be better to just remove it outright than decomission it, putting in an OOC note to explain why. This puts down unnecessary canon, and just feels sad.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm assuming you haven't read what <a href="/scp-076">SCP-076</a> looks like these days? This is both a key cultural aspect of the site as well as underlining the reason why we don't put humanoid SCPs to use. It is an important entry and was vetted by several administrators, so it's not likely to be removed or changed regardless of whether you feel that way or not.</p>

