<p>No. You just didn't read the old version.</p>
<p><strong>Pandora's Box is decommissioned on the old version</strong>. All we did was expand the description of it a little. We specifically decided we didn't <em>want</em> to remove it outright. It's just in line with the current 076 article, as Aelanna pointed out.</p>
<p>In fact, Clef crossed off the entry and added the note before you even posted once on this site, in November 2011. (I checked purely out of curiosity because that error was so fucking weird.) In fact, it was done the very same day that we gave Task Forces their own page.</p>
<p>Link: <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-412447/task-forces-arc#post-1308170">http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-412447/task-forces-arc#post-1308170</a></p>
<p>It's fine to have problems with something, but it would be nice to not make up problems out of whole cloth. All you're demonstrating is that the old version was completely ignored by anyone that didn't have a personal pet task force on it. :P</p>
<p>EDIT: And, yeah, it seems really strange to call this rigid. We went through a lot of effort to encompass &#8230; pretty much every popular interpretation. Whereas the previous concept was &quot;extremely tiny groups of soldiers, only&quot;. Those are covered by this page too, incidentally.</p>

