<p>They're CSS magic code. They weren't drawn, or found &#8212; they were designed by Aelanna.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Alpha-1: So wait, the O5s actually do play a role in skip containment? And if this group is so top-secret, why is it listed here?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not top-secret, and Red Right Hand doesn't necessarily play a role in skip containment. It's just top secret what <em>specifically</em> it is that they do. Everyone who knows about them or reads some version of this document in-universe knows that they work for the O5 Council and answer to <em>no one else</em>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Gamma-5 and Gamma-6: I'm pretty sure that there are more then six aquatic SCPs. If a new one were to pop up, would one of them send a couple of members, or would the entire force go and temporarily leave the skips in ongoing containment to the foundation?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This list of MTFs is quite intentionally incomplete, and says so&#8230;. repeatedly. ;)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Nu-7: You are aware that if the mary-sue-writers out there find this task force, it'll be used in half the articles in the draft section. Every newbie will want their skip to be good enough to deserve Nu-7.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's not really anything wrong with this. If a skip including Nu-7 is bad, it won't be bad because of Nu-7.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I understand that the Foundation needs to be discreet and not cause the masses to panic, but this is a little ridiculous. I mean yeah, they could pose as a construction team and knock down a old, abandoned house, but what about a house that is actively occupied by a family?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Dude&#8230; you specifically cut out the &quot;<strong>and/or</strong>&quot; in your comment, which is a little strange, because it answers your question. :p They don't knock down every single house, they demolish the ones they can or must demolish.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Yeah, because the Foundation just wants to track a drooling, flesh-hungry zombie, rather then containing it (Sorry to be a bit blunt).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And again you cut out the &quot;and/or&quot;. This comment is getting weird as hell, man. You're quoting sentences that have the answer to your issue literally snipped out of them&#8230; by you. Why?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Omega-7: I get that this is a rather embarrassing, mary-sue-ish part of the site's history, but why leave it on there then? Why not just delete all the pages related to it?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why on earth would we do that?</p>
<p>And, that assumes that we're actually embarrassed by it. I, personally, enjoy Omega-7 and its related material, including its tragic end. As do many, many other people.</p>
<p>We could delete the entry, but that's less fun. It would, in my opinion, make the list more boring.</p>

							</div>

								
					
